From 2977d14ce19d5ba71742f32084570b207de5148e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Signbot AutoDL <zhengsw200304@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Add path-configurable data pipeline for How2Sign/SOKE
 SMPL-X poses

tools/prepare_smplx_poses.py   SMPL-X pkl -> source_body/*.npy + hand_joints/*.npz
tools/generate_motion_yaml.py  index.csv -> motion yaml (absolute root + hand_root)
tools/retarget_hands.py        hand joints -> Linker hand angles (dex-retargeting env)
retarget_motion_h1_smpl.py     argparse, bounded worker count, per-clip error handling

Fixes vs upstream data_process_body.py / data_process_hand.py:
- How2Sign frames (<clip>_<i>_3D.pkl) were sorted lexicographically -> scrambled.
- lower-body template S000003_P0000_T00.npy is not in the repo; use a canonical
  upright template (or --template).
- SMPL-X model built once and run batched instead of per frame per clip.
- body and hand come from one forward pass, so frame counts always match.
Default training motion yaml -> motions_how2sign_val.yaml.
